<task id="040" project="spaarkeai-compose-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-17 in-editor find/replace (case-sensitivity + replace-all; tracked-changes-mark-safe)</title>
    <phase>4 Toolset</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W4-Toolset</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>frontend,tiptap,fluent-ui</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
    <assigned>unassigned</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement FR-17: in-editor find and replace for the Compose editor. The find field highlights all
    matches; a case-sensitivity toggle scopes matching; replace and replace-all mutate the document. The
    load-bearing constraint is that find/replace MUST interoperate with the existing tracked-changes marks
    (`InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark`/`CommentAnchorMark`) WITHOUT corrupting them — a replace that lands on a
    marked range must preserve or correctly re-apply those marks, never strip or orphan them. Build this
    small and self-contained on the MIT TipTap base — NO `@tiptap-pro/*`, no TipTap product "Search &amp;
    Replace Pro" module, no MIT-Pro dependency (design §7.5 lists this as "Build (small; no MIT-Pro
    dependency)"). A ProseMirror decoration-based highlight pass plus a replace transaction that respects
    stored marks is the pattern.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/TypeScript engineer fluent in TipTap 3 / ProseMirror (decorations, transactions, mark
    handling) and Fluent UI v9. Comfortable reasoning about how a text-replacement transaction interacts
    with inline marks so that tracked-changes annotations survive edits intact.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A find/replace UI surface wired into `ComposeEditor.tsx` (via a new dedicated component + a small
    hook) that: highlights all matches with an optional case-sensitivity toggle; supports replace (current
    match) and replace-all; and drives replacement through a ProseMirror transaction that leaves the
    Compose tracked-changes marks uncorrupted. Matching unit/component tests assert the highlight, the
    case-sensitivity scoping, replace-all correctness, and mark-integrity after a replace over a marked
    range, plus an ADR-021 dark-mode render check.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §7.5 "The Editing Surface" lists find/replace as a table-stakes credibility tool to BUILD
      (small; no MIT-Pro dependency) — "a common credibility gap today." The editor already owns the
      hard part: native `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment` marks. Find/replace is an everyday tool layered on
      the MIT base. This is a client-only task (no BFF surface, no save-path change) and is independent of
      the E1/E2 fidelity core, so it runs in the W4 parallel toolset wave.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx — mount the find/replace surface + register any editor extension/decoration plugin for match highlighting</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeFindReplace.tsx — NEW Fluent v9 find/replace panel (find field, replace field, case-sensitivity toggle, prev/next, replace, replace-all)</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useComposeFindReplace.ts — NEW hook: match search over editor doc, decoration highlight, replace + replace-all transactions that preserve marks</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/marks/InsertionMark.ts — tracked-change insertion mark; a replace must not corrupt it</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/marks/DeletionMark.ts — tracked-change deletion mark; must survive replace</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/marks/CommentAnchorMark.ts — comment anchor mark; must survive replace</file>
      <file role="reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/marks/QaHighlightExtension.ts — existing ProseMirror decoration-based highlight extension; mirror this pattern for match highlighting</file>
      <file role="reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx — existing Fluent v9 editor toolbar; mirror its component conventions + theming</file>
      <file role="export">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/index.ts — export the new component if it is part of the public surface</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §7.5 (The Editing Surface — find/replace = Build, small); spec.md FR-17</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">Independent — no task dependency. Runs in the W4 toolset parallel wave alongside 042/043/044.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project / owner rule 2026-07-14">NO TipTap product feature (paid or unpaid) — no "Search &amp; Replace Pro" or any `@tiptap-pro/*` module. Build on the MIT TipTap base / ProseMirror primitives / our own code only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03 / project">If any npm extension is added, verify it resolves to `@tiptap/extension-*` (MIT), NEVER `@tiptap-pro/*`. Prefer zero new dependency (decoration + transaction primitives already available).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-17 / project">Find/replace MUST interoperate with the tracked-changes marks (`InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark`/`CommentAnchorMark`) WITHOUT corrupting them. A replace over a marked range must preserve or correctly re-apply the marks — never strip, split incorrectly, or orphan them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021 / NFR-10">All new UI is Fluent UI v9 and MUST render correctly in dark mode (theme tokens, no hard-coded colors).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / NFR-10">Any client fetch (none expected here) uses `@spaarke/auth`; do not hand-roll auth headers. This task is editor-local and should add no network calls.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Client component/unit tests only (no BFF); no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests. Tests must exercise real editor state (highlight, replace-all, mark integrity).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">New component — provide the `&lt;justification&gt;` (Existing / Extension / Cost-of-doing-nothing).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>TipTap 3 / ProseMirror decorations + mark-preserving replace transactions; Fluent v9 editor UI + dark mode</topic>
    <files>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
