      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-theming.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Decoration-based highlight" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/marks/QaHighlightExtension.ts">
        Existing ProseMirror decoration extension that highlights ranges without mutating the doc — mirror this for find-match highlighting so matches are visual-only until replace.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Fluent v9 editor toolbar surface" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx">
        Existing Fluent v9 toolbar; copy its component structure, token usage, and dark-mode-safe styling for the find/replace panel.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor. Load the knowledge files + design §7.5. Read the three mark files and `QaHighlightExtension.ts` to understand how marks and decorations coexist.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Match search + highlight">Implement the search pass in `useComposeFindReplace.ts`: iterate the editor doc text, honor the case-sensitivity toggle, and render matches as ProseMirror decorations (mirroring `QaHighlightExtension`). No doc mutation on find.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Replace + replace-all transactions">Implement replace (current match) and replace-all as ProseMirror transactions. When a match range carries `InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark`/`CommentAnchorMark`, preserve/re-apply the marks on the replacement text so tracked changes are not corrupted or orphaned.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Fluent v9 panel">Build `ComposeFindReplace.tsx`: find field, replace field, case-sensitivity toggle, prev/next navigation, replace, replace-all. Use Fluent v9 tokens; verify dark mode. Mirror `ComposeFormatToolbar` conventions.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Wire into editor">Mount the panel in `ComposeEditor.tsx` (toggleable), register the highlight decoration plugin, and export from `index.ts` if public.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Tests">Author component/unit tests: highlight count, case-sensitivity scoping, replace-all correctness, and the mark-integrity assertion (replace over a `InsertionMark` range keeps the mark intact). Include an ADR-021 dark-mode render check.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Verify">`npm run build` the shared lib; run the new tests. Update TASK-INDEX status.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeFindReplace.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useComposeFindReplace.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx (find/replace mounted + highlight plugin registered)</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeFindReplace.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>

  <justification>
    <existing>No existing find/replace surface. `QaHighlightExtension.ts` highlights QA ranges only (read-only, single-purpose); `ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx` is formatting buttons. Neither searches text or replaces.</existing>
    <extension>Cannot fold into `ComposeFormatToolbar` (that is inline formatting, a distinct concern) nor into `QaHighlightExtension` (a QA-specific read-only decoration). Find/replace is a cohesive interactive tool with its own search/replace state that warrants a dedicated component + hook.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, the editor lacks a table-stakes 2026 credibility tool (design §7.5) — a maker cannot do a bulk term change (e.g. rename a defined party across a contract) without leaving Compose. Concrete failing contract: FR-17 acceptance "find highlights matches; replace-all updates all; interoperates with tracked-changes marks without corrupting them" cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Entering a term in the find field highlights all matches in the editor; clearing the term removes the highlights (decoration-only, no doc mutation).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The case-sensitivity toggle scopes matching: with it on, only exact-case matches highlight; with it off, matches are case-insensitive.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Replace-all replaces every match with the replacement text in a single logical operation; a unit test asserts the resulting document text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A replace that lands on a range carrying `InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark`/`CommentAnchorMark` preserves those marks on the replacement text — a unit test asserts the marks remain intact and are not orphaned or stripped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `@tiptap-pro/*` dependency and no TipTap product feature is added; any npm extension used resolves to `@tiptap/extension-*` (MIT). Ideally zero new dependency.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The find/replace panel renders correctly in Fluent v9 dark mode (theme tokens; no hard-coded colors) — ADR-021.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Matching component tests exist and pass; shared-lib `npm run build` is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="Find highlights matches">
      <steps>Open a doc with repeated term "Agreement". Type "Agreement" in the find field.</steps>
      <expected>All occurrences highlight; a match count reflects the number found; no document text changes.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Case-sensitivity scopes matching">
      <steps>With a doc containing "Party" and "party", toggle case-sensitivity ON and search "Party".</steps>
      <expected>Only the capital-P "Party" occurrences highlight; toggling OFF highlights both casings.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Replace-all updates all matches">
      <steps>Search "Acme" (3 occurrences), enter replacement "Globex", click Replace All.</steps>
      <expected>All three occurrences become "Globex"; editor text reflects the change.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Replace over tracked-change mark preserves it">
      <steps>Place an `InsertionMark` over a phrase, then replace that phrase via find/replace.</steps>
      <expected>The replacement text still carries the insertion mark; the tracked change is not corrupted or removed.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps>Render the find/replace panel under the Fluent v9 dark theme provider.</steps>
      <expected>Panel, fields, toggle, and buttons use theme tokens and are legible in dark mode; no hard-coded light colors.</expected>
    </ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
